{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Root cause confirmed by 2-clone reproduction: rebuild_snapshot_under_lock placed the rebuilt SNAPSHOT at hlc.next_tick (repair clock); fsck does not fetch, so a tag written on clone B 24 s before the repair merged in before the SNAPSHOT, uncited (ORPHAN_EVENT). Fix reuses compact_txn._snapshot_timestamp with the configured horizon and no young events; anchor is the newest RAW source (not a prior clock-placed SNAPSHOT). Unreadable config aborts before mutation. Tests: 3 new positive-horizon/abort tests fail before (3 failed, 5 passed) and pass after (8 passed); 688 passed, 2 skipped across compact/fsck/fold/rebuild/snapshot modules; make lint and make typecheck exit 0; rebuild_snapshot_under_lock complexity unchanged at 12. Gerrit change 3308."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793814254232854001,"uuid":"0d3b268e-cdfd-489c-877b-211cf97d26f2"}